translate.glossary:
Prepare the glossary for translating the book "{title}" into {dst}.
Return STRICTLY valid JSON without a markdown fence:
{{
  "title": "the book title in {dst}",
  "names": {{"<name in the original>": "<name in {dst}>"}},
  "chapter_titles": {{"<chapter title in the original>": "<chapter title in {dst}>"}},
  "chapter_heading": "the natural chapter-heading format in {dst}, keeping the {{n}} (number) and {{title}} placeholders",
  "act_heading": "the natural act-heading format in {dst} with the {{n}} placeholder"
}}

Rules for names: transliterate personal names by the accepted {dst} conventions; translate meaningful (speaking) names so the meaning survives; real-world names and places take their established {dst} forms. EVERY name listed below must appear as a key in "names".

Names (characters, locations, key terms):
{names}

Chapter titles:
{chapters}
